          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Plato</strong><br>\nPlato was born in Athens, around 428 BCE, into a well-to-do and politically active family. His real name was Aristocles, but he was dubbed \"Plato\" because of his broad physical build. The political climate of Athens influenced his thoughts profoundly, as he lived through the Peloponnesian War and the subsequent overthrow of the democratic government. Plato was a student of Socrates, whose methods of dialogue and skepticism laid the foundation for Plato's own exploration of philosophical ideas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Plato's Academy</strong><br>\nIn 387 BCE, Plato founded the Academy in Athens, one of the earliest known organized schools in Western civilization. It was here that he taught Aristotle, who would also become a famous philosopher. The Academy served as a center for research and instruction in philosophy and the sciences. It remained active for about three centuries after Plato's death, testament to the durability of his educational legacy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Theory of Forms</strong><br>\nPlato is best known for his Theory of Forms, which proposes that non-material abstract forms, and not the material world of change known to us through sensation, possess the highest and most fundamental kind of reality. According to Plato, objects in our world are merely shadows of these pure forms. For instance, all circular objects are imperfect copies of the \"Form of the Circle\" which exists in an immaterial realm.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
